  "profile": "corporate",
  "notes": "SABIC Agri-Nutrients Company (SABIC AN, formerly SAFCO; ticker 2020) audited consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/382_0_2026-03-03...). Auditor PwC. Board of Directors authorised issue on 09 Ramadan 1447H / 26 February 2026 (used as filed_at). The filed PDF's primary statements and notes are digital text; the statement of financial position, statement of income and cash-flow statement were cross-read from page images because the two-column PwC layout mis-aligns on plain text extraction. Amounts are in thousands of Saudi Riyals (scale 1000). SABIC AN is 50.1% owned by SABIC (2010). income_taxes_and_zakat sums the reported 'Zakat expense', 'Income tax expense' and 'Deferred tax (expense) credit' lines (also carried split as zakat_expense / income_tax_expense / deferred_tax_expense). operating_income is the reported 'Income from operations'. additional_paid_in_capital is 'Share premium'. long_term_investments is 'Investments in equity instruments'; investments_associates is 'Investments in an associate and a joint venture'. other_noncurrent_liabilities is the non-current 'Derivative financial instrument' (a symmetrical put/call option over Al-Bayroni NCI, carried at fair value with movements booked to retained earnings). defined_benefit_obligation is the non-current 'Employee benefits'; employee_benefits_current is the current portion. There is no bank debt - the only interest-bearing liabilities are IFRS 16 leases. depreciation_amortization sums depreciation of property, plant and equipment, depreciation of right-of-use assets and amortisation of intangible assets from the cash-flow statement. capex is 'Purchase of property, plant and equipment'. interest_paid is 'Finance cost paid'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat and income tax paid'; dividends_paid is the shareholder dividend (NCI dividends of SAR 76,540 thousand excluded). The cash-flow statement reconciles with no separate foreign-exchange effect line. Statement page references are the printed page numbers: financial position 7, income 8, comprehensive income 9, changes in equity 10, cash flows 11-12.",
